WEBVTT

00:00.510 --> 00:02.480
Hey, you're here.

00:03.220 --> 00:05.430
It's everyone from Lion Fang.

00:05.430 --> 00:07.350
Takumi, you came.

00:07.350 --> 00:09.660
What's going on in Wedgefort?

00:09.940 --> 00:12.610
A horde of monsters is stampeding toward it.

00:13.000 --> 00:14.570
A stampede of monsters?

00:14.930 --> 00:19.050
Some say they're being lured by 
the presence of people in Wedgefort.

00:19.050 --> 00:22.030
Captain Dorn has asked for our assistance.

00:22.030 --> 00:25.960
Given what we're up against, we've only 
summoned rank B and higher adveturers,

00:25.960 --> 00:27.380
but the timing is not in our favor.

00:27.380 --> 00:29.170
What do you mean?

00:29.170 --> 00:32.500
Apparently, most parties 
are out on other quests.

00:32.500 --> 00:35.720
Then you mean it's just us?

00:35.720 --> 00:39.470
Well, at least the three parties 
that happened to be around

00:39.470 --> 00:42.180
are capable of doing the work of a hundred.

00:42.630 --> 00:44.140
Hold it right there!

00:44.140 --> 00:45.390
Three...

00:45.390 --> 00:48.600
Are you telling me <i>they're</i> here, too?

00:48.600 --> 00:53.200
Yeah. Lion Fang, the Wings of Nolyn, and...

00:53.810 --> 00:55.590
The Crimson Rose.

00:55.740 --> 01:00.530
<b>Crimson Rose, Merilda</b>

00:57.020 --> 00:59.690
I'm the leader of the Crimson Rose, Merilda.

00:59.690 --> 01:00.540
Nice to meet you.

01:00.530 --> 01:03.000
<b>Baralai</b>

01:00.540 --> 01:02.300
This is our tank, Baralai,

01:03.000 --> 01:04.900
our mage, Mary,

01:03.000 --> 01:05.460
<b>Mary</b>

01:05.460 --> 01:08.920
<b>Linda</b>

01:05.460 --> 01:08.920
<b>Paula</b>

01:05.820 --> 01:07.260
our healer, Paula,

01:07.260 --> 01:08.920
and our scout, Linda.

01:09.330 --> 01:12.480
We've heard the rumors 
about the Wings of Nolyn.

01:12.480 --> 01:14.030
You must be Sofia.

01:14.370 --> 01:16.920
Of course it's you all.

01:16.920 --> 01:18.390
It's been a while.

01:18.610 --> 01:22.130
I've heard you two have still 
been active as Lion Fang.

01:22.130 --> 01:25.120
Hey! There's <i>three</i> of us in Lion Fang!

01:25.120 --> 01:27.670
Oh, Riell. You're still alive?

01:27.670 --> 01:28.900
Hah!

01:28.900 --> 01:30.200
Man...

01:30.200 --> 01:33.120
This is why I can't stand you all.

01:33.910 --> 01:37.080
Captain Dorn will be leadin' a 
squad of knights there soon.

01:37.320 --> 01:41.910
Takumi, go with Lion Fang and 
Crimson Rose ahead of 'em.

01:41.910 --> 01:43.010
Alright!

03:15.540 --> 03:20.550
<b>Episode 12
When Bonds Are Tested</b>

03:15.540 --> 03:20.550
<b>Episode 12
When Bonds Are Tested</b>

03:16.540 --> 03:20.580
<i>We all left for Wedgefort immediately.</i>

03:21.230 --> 03:24.330
<i>We left Akane and Lulu behind at the mansion,</i>

03:24.690 --> 03:26.690
<i>and assigned Titan to guard them.</i>

03:30.620 --> 03:34.050
This is the Holy Sword Amaterasu 
that I just synthesized recently.

03:34.670 --> 03:39.540
It's made from the orichalcum
we obtained in that dungeon.

03:39.540 --> 03:41.250
Orihalcum...

03:41.250 --> 03:43.330
I'd like you to use it, Sofia.

03:44.140 --> 03:46.560
It's something of a sister sword

03:46.560 --> 03:49.460
to the other one I synthesized, 
the Sublime Sword Tsukuyomi.

03:50.680 --> 03:53.880
While Amaterasu delivers 
devastating damage to its foes,

03:53.880 --> 03:56.920
Tsukuyomi inflicts mental damage 
from even the slightest scratches.

03:57.680 --> 04:00.210
If we can chain attacks
from these two swords,

04:00.210 --> 04:02.450
it should prove quite efficient.

04:02.450 --> 04:03.680
Chain them?

04:04.130 --> 04:07.350
It means we'll need teamwork.

04:08.770 --> 04:10.070
Can I count on you?

04:12.060 --> 04:13.770
The honor is mine.

04:14.560 --> 04:17.220
Wedgefort should be coming into view soon.

04:17.220 --> 04:19.150
It's almost dawn.

04:19.150 --> 04:22.370
Now to find out what we're walking into.

04:23.160 --> 04:27.770
There aren't that many monsters that 
can get over those tall ramparts.

04:27.770 --> 04:29.660
I'm sure they'll be fine.

04:30.860 --> 04:32.770
Master! Bad news!

04:43.710 --> 04:45.850
Winged monsters?!

04:45.850 --> 04:47.970
They're passing over the ramparts?!

04:47.970 --> 04:50.830
We can't dawdle around, now can we!

04:50.830 --> 04:51.810
Riell!

04:58.530 --> 04:59.960
Thor's Hammer!

05:00.480 --> 05:01.450
Tornado!

05:13.450 --> 05:14.790
Camellia!

05:26.130 --> 05:28.800
Oh! It's Mr. Iruma!

05:28.800 --> 05:30.590
Lower the drawbridge!

05:33.590 --> 05:36.120
Takumi, leave this area to us!

05:36.120 --> 05:38.740
We'll go the opposite way 
around the ramparts!

05:39.190 --> 05:40.410
Thank you!

05:56.770 --> 06:00.060
That's every monster inside the walls.

06:00.060 --> 06:00.840
Yes.

06:01.360 --> 06:03.290
Mr. Takumi! Mr. Takumi!

06:03.290 --> 06:05.080
Sofia!

06:05.080 --> 06:06.710
Maria! Reyva!

06:06.710 --> 06:07.770
Máni!

06:08.030 --> 06:10.780
You've all done well protecting the village.

06:10.780 --> 06:12.730
Because we had faith in you all!

06:13.630 --> 06:16.650
Reyva and Máni, please treat the injured.

06:17.260 --> 06:21.850
Sofia and Maria, come with me and Maple 
to back up Heath and the others!

06:24.590 --> 06:26.320
Sorry we're late!

06:26.520 --> 06:27.380
Look.

06:32.020 --> 06:33.410
They're going into the woods?

06:33.410 --> 06:35.340
Does this mean they're retreating?

06:36.040 --> 06:38.000
And all at once, too.

06:38.000 --> 06:39.170
All at once?

06:39.170 --> 06:44.650
It's almost like the monsters are
coordinating their movements.

06:44.650 --> 06:46.590
No way.

06:46.590 --> 06:48.310
Monsters can't work together.

06:48.850 --> 06:52.850
Yet just when we thought they were 
attacking, they've pulled back,

06:53.300 --> 06:57.810
and then attacked again when 
we were resting, over and over.

06:58.070 --> 07:01.810
Maybe there's some kind of 
leader among the monsters.

07:01.810 --> 07:04.030
A monster capable of leading other monsters?

07:04.030 --> 07:06.370
I've never seen anything like that before.

07:06.840 --> 07:08.910
There's one reason I can think of.

07:09.550 --> 07:13.240
When Sidonia summoned the 
heroes several months ago,

07:13.630 --> 07:16.200
we felt a large fluctuation of mana.

07:17.560 --> 07:23.750
Is it possible it caused 
some monsters to evolve?

07:24.750 --> 07:28.510
Are you saying that surge of mana was 
large enough to cause evolution?

07:29.140 --> 07:33.520
The summoning spell is powerful 
enough that Lady Nolyn forbade it.

07:34.030 --> 07:37.090
It wouldn't be a surprise if 
it affected the monsters.

07:37.690 --> 07:42.440
Apparently this monster extermination 
isn't going to be like the rest.

07:46.020 --> 07:51.030
<b>Holy Empire of Sidonia</b>

07:46.700 --> 07:51.640
A stampede of monsters is attacking the 
fortress near the Kingdom of Barcula?

07:52.020 --> 07:52.910
Yes.

07:52.910 --> 07:57.150
We've received reports that the monsters 
number enough to wipe out a nation.

07:57.150 --> 08:02.750
And if they were to destroy the fortress 
and invade the lands of Barcula?

08:03.050 --> 08:06.850
Damage that would tip the balance of power 
among nations would be unavoidable.

08:07.220 --> 08:10.480
Makes you want to support 
the monsters, doesn't it?

08:10.480 --> 08:11.170
Indeed.

08:11.170 --> 08:13.460
We must act on this opportunity.

08:13.460 --> 08:16.910
Ready the troops to deploy
at a moment's notice.

08:16.910 --> 08:18.090
Father.

08:18.090 --> 08:23.470
Why not take this chance to deal damage 
to the nations allied with Barcula?

08:24.240 --> 08:26.250
You mean the Kingdom of Samandor?

08:27.130 --> 08:30.670
We should render them incapable of lending 
Barcula aid when the time comes,

08:30.670 --> 08:32.240
so we must strike first.

08:32.240 --> 08:34.610
Hm... And how?

08:34.890 --> 08:37.870
With the heroes, of course.

08:46.450 --> 08:48.990
<i>There are more injured
than I had anticipated.</i>

08:51.240 --> 08:52.840
Here's your meal.

08:55.360 --> 08:56.480
Thank you.

08:58.480 --> 08:59.840
What's wrong?

08:59.840 --> 09:01.480
It's Mr. Takumi.

09:01.480 --> 09:03.300
I'm worried about him.

09:06.010 --> 09:09.980
He's providing every potion 
we have to the injured.

09:10.740 --> 09:12.900
Do we not have any in storage?

09:12.900 --> 09:16.950
We just delivered the 
Papek Company's order the other day,

09:17.240 --> 09:20.310
and we haven't had the time 
to start on the next batch.

09:25.500 --> 09:29.480
Potions are only worth 
anything when used, Sofia.

09:29.480 --> 09:32.590
However, the monsters will be 
attacking again after this.

09:32.590 --> 09:34.950
At least keep some to use for yourself.

09:35.660 --> 09:39.000
I just need to avoid any injuries
 that would require taking a potion,

09:39.920 --> 09:41.650
and I can moderate my stamina use.

09:42.050 --> 09:43.670
Mr. Takumi.

09:46.700 --> 09:49.510
<i>This is the man Takumi Iruma is.</i>

09:50.230 --> 09:53.460
<i>He'll prioritize the wounded over himself.</i>

09:53.460 --> 09:57.260
<i>Though I swore my loyalty to him 
precisely because that is who he is!</i>

09:58.760 --> 10:00.690
<i>I'll protect Mr. Takumi.</i>

10:01.100 --> 10:02.830
<i>Even if it costs my life!</i>

10:04.950 --> 10:08.660
Gather the children in one place 
and keep them from going outside.

10:08.660 --> 10:12.120
Reyva, Máni, Maple, guard the children.

10:12.350 --> 10:13.630
Yes.

10:13.630 --> 10:14.830
Got it!

10:15.950 --> 10:17.290
<i>Master!</i>

10:17.730 --> 10:20.300
<i>The forest is stirring again!</i>

10:22.060 --> 10:23.980
Takumi, what's the strategy?

10:24.280 --> 10:26.530
It's not worth calling a strategy,

10:27.350 --> 10:30.890
but first we'll rain down magic, 
then I'll have Camellia charge in.

10:31.910 --> 10:35.620
After that, I plan to slaughter 
any I can get my hands on.

10:36.080 --> 10:38.050
I think that's a good offensive.

10:38.050 --> 10:41.350
It'll be best for each of our parties 
to work together and take them down.

10:46.190 --> 10:48.290
There are more of them than ever before!

10:52.010 --> 10:54.460
They may be launching an all-out attack.

10:54.460 --> 10:56.970
Mary, it's almost time.

11:05.100 --> 11:06.310
Thor's Hammer!

11:06.310 --> 11:07.180
Tornado!

11:07.180 --> 11:08.560
Fire Storm!

11:09.060 --> 11:10.340
Foxfire Barrage!

11:10.340 --> 11:12.020
Fire Storm!

11:17.990 --> 11:19.040
Camellia!

11:19.900 --> 11:21.860
Let's go!

11:47.750 --> 11:49.830
I'm going to protect the children!

11:49.830 --> 11:50.920
Go!

11:53.310 --> 11:56.180
Takumi, we'll go left!

11:57.380 --> 11:59.900
Crimson Rose will take the right!

12:06.410 --> 12:07.530
Sofia!

12:08.370 --> 12:09.550
Tornado!

12:16.470 --> 12:17.530
Sofia!

12:17.530 --> 12:19.220
You're advancing too quickly! Come back!

12:19.220 --> 12:20.370
It's fine!

12:31.180 --> 12:33.910
<i>The monsters fell back?</i>

13:03.600 --> 13:05.370
This is their leader?!

13:16.960 --> 13:19.320
I should've brought Titan with us!

13:22.280 --> 13:24.380
Over here, you big lizard!

13:24.380 --> 13:25.990
Sofia, stop!

13:25.990 --> 13:28.460
Come here! Over here!

13:42.010 --> 13:43.470
Sofia!

14:01.490 --> 14:02.860
Thor's Hammer!

14:03.460 --> 14:04.570
Tornado!

14:13.220 --> 14:14.470
Mr. Takumi!

14:17.280 --> 14:18.750
Amaterasu!

14:22.520 --> 14:24.010
Tsukuyomi!

14:25.950 --> 14:28.600
<i>Give it all the mana I have left!</i>

14:44.640 --> 14:46.450
He did it!

14:54.110 --> 14:55.140
Heal.

14:56.470 --> 14:59.630
Tend to yourself before me.

15:00.260 --> 15:03.000
Why... were you so reckless?

15:05.160 --> 15:07.630
I just wanted...

15:07.630 --> 15:09.920
to protect you.

15:10.210 --> 15:13.390
Sofia, you could've died.

15:13.670 --> 15:17.610
If Maria and the others had arrived 
even a moment later...

15:18.110 --> 15:19.810
My life isn't worth that much.

15:21.480 --> 15:24.720
You shouldn't... throw your life away.

15:34.180 --> 15:35.260
What's wrong?

15:35.640 --> 15:37.990
What happened to the other monsters?

15:37.990 --> 15:40.070
They've turned tail and fled.

15:40.430 --> 15:42.460
We've defeated all the stragglers.

15:43.180 --> 15:46.150
That's good.

15:46.840 --> 15:48.260
Mr. Takumi?

15:48.260 --> 15:50.020
Mr. Takumi!

15:58.180 --> 15:59.560
Mr. Takumi!

15:59.560 --> 16:00.630
Master!

16:00.630 --> 16:03.600
Mr. Takumi is awake!

16:03.600 --> 16:06.220
Thank goodness.

16:06.220 --> 16:08.760
I was worried about Mr. Takumi.

16:08.760 --> 16:12.330
Your leader really is an impressive man.

16:15.560 --> 16:21.740
<i>Several days later, we returned to Bolton 
after helping the village rebuild.</i>

16:25.000 --> 16:27.660
I feel <i>much</i> better.

16:27.660 --> 16:29.960
I still haven't had enough action.

16:30.220 --> 16:33.640
We can manage just fine,
even without Akane!

16:35.070 --> 16:37.680
Because we're the heroes!

16:47.070 --> 16:49.310
Please eat up.

16:49.680 --> 16:52.330
There's plenty more.

16:52.790 --> 16:54.490
Meat!

16:54.730 --> 16:57.190
Meat! Meat!

16:58.370 --> 16:59.670
Maria.

17:05.380 --> 17:07.910
What's wrong with Sofia?

17:07.910 --> 17:12.170
She's been like that since 
we returned from Wedgefort.

17:16.450 --> 17:17.280
Huh?

17:17.280 --> 17:18.250
What?

17:18.250 --> 17:23.230
Why do you think we're
throwing a party?

17:28.640 --> 17:30.870
Stare.

17:33.230 --> 17:34.270
Right.

17:39.180 --> 17:42.400
I can't believe I took such an 
oppressive attitude with Mr. Takumi!

17:42.400 --> 17:48.710
I'm even lower than a 
toilet regurgitating water!

17:50.070 --> 17:51.370
It's freshly roasted.

17:52.020 --> 17:54.330
Mr. Takumi?

17:59.230 --> 18:01.580
I'm sorry for shouting at you like that.

18:02.050 --> 18:02.870
No...

18:03.950 --> 18:05.670
I was in the wrong.

18:07.140 --> 18:11.750
You took that reckless action to protect me.

18:11.750 --> 18:12.870
I know that.

18:13.460 --> 18:17.150
I wanted to protect you,

18:17.150 --> 18:18.860
even if it cost my life.

18:18.860 --> 18:21.200
I'm grateful for that sentiment,

18:21.200 --> 18:26.760
but I don't want you to 
sacrifice yourself, Sofia.

18:26.760 --> 18:28.800
We both rely on and support each other.

18:28.800 --> 18:30.650
We both believe in each other.

18:31.130 --> 18:35.220
That's the kind of partners I want us to be.

18:38.070 --> 18:41.170
I want you to live, and be by my side.

18:41.730 --> 18:43.380
Forever, if possible.

18:43.850 --> 18:47.030
Mr. Takumi...

18:48.630 --> 18:51.850
If you're okay with that, that is.

18:53.960 --> 18:56.790
I'll stay with you forever.

19:03.990 --> 19:05.770
The meat's ready!

19:05.770 --> 19:09.240
Ah, Akane, they were...

19:10.310 --> 19:13.730
C'mon! Let's eat together already!

19:11.120 --> 19:14.030
...just getting into a good mood.

19:13.730 --> 19:16.410
You didn't have to bring it up right <i>now!</i>

19:14.500 --> 19:17.380
What an impeccable lack of awareness.

19:16.410 --> 19:19.250
We should eat while it's hot!

19:18.200 --> 19:20.470
I'm so sorry.

19:22.010 --> 19:23.240
<i>Several days later...</i>

19:24.030 --> 19:26.430
<i>I took Akane and Lulu to visit the lord,</i>

19:26.430 --> 19:31.330
<i>and asked if I could harbor them 
in my mansion for a while.</i>

19:31.950 --> 19:37.940
<i>The lord agreed, and now they'll 
be staying with us.</i>

19:38.580 --> 19:43.030
<i>The lord also told me about the massacre 
of a village in the Kingdom of Samandor,</i>

19:43.820 --> 19:48.000
<i>along with the fact that Sidonia's 
two heroes were behind it.</i>

19:49.810 --> 19:51.310
Akane?

19:52.250 --> 19:53.550
If I...

19:53.550 --> 19:56.420
If I had stopped those two...

19:57.300 --> 19:59.020
If I had been with them...

19:59.020 --> 20:00.620
It's not your fault.

20:01.730 --> 20:07.100
At some point in the future, 
I'll have to face those two.

20:07.630 --> 20:08.590
But...

20:10.110 --> 20:11.100
Next time...

20:12.390 --> 20:13.880
I won't run!

20:16.140 --> 20:21.820
<i>Sidonia has forced this innocent 
girl to shoulder a heavy fate</i>

20:21.820 --> 20:24.330
<i>for the sake of its selfish ambitions.</i>

20:25.900 --> 20:27.700
Long time, no see!

20:28.660 --> 20:29.860
Lady Nolyn.

20:30.270 --> 20:33.460
There was a reason that 
you sent me a year before

20:33.460 --> 20:35.370
of the hero summoning, wasn't there?

20:35.660 --> 20:37.380
The Heroes, Sidonia...

20:37.380 --> 20:40.020
They're steadily growing more 
entangled with my life.

20:40.560 --> 20:43.720
You have some kind of plan, 
don't you, Lady Nolyn?

20:44.080 --> 20:45.310
I told you, right?

20:45.310 --> 20:47.800
It's all up to you.

20:49.650 --> 20:50.790
Just one thing.

20:51.220 --> 20:55.640
I will protect what's precious 
to me in this world.

20:56.390 --> 20:57.490
No matter what.

20:58.330 --> 21:02.990
After all, as an alchemist, I get to 
create all the things I could ever want!

21:02.990 --> 21:05.240
It's the greatest life ever!

21:05.740 --> 21:09.170
I really like the life I have now.

21:09.950 --> 21:10.980
Mm-hmm.

21:11.960 --> 21:12.970
Here.

21:13.470 --> 21:15.920
The sweets you requested.

21:17.570 --> 21:19.640
Good! I'm satisfied.

21:21.800 --> 21:22.580
<i>Takumi.</i>

21:23.830 --> 21:27.460
<i>The fate awaiting you isn't an easy one.</i>

21:28.420 --> 21:32.120
<i>You are the sole hope for Mildgard.</i>

21:33.720 --> 21:37.170
<i>If you grow strong, 
then the future will change.</i>

21:38.150 --> 21:40.890
<i>I'm counting on you, Takumi Iruma.</i>

21:42.590 --> 21:43.440
<i>One day,</i>

21:44.250 --> 21:47.560
<i>you could possibly be the 
greatest alchemist of all time.</i>

